.TH KOSH 5 "2026-08-04" "kosh" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
kosh \- shell startup configuration files
.SH DESCRIPTION
The startup configuration files contain shell commands. Each file is parsed
with the grammar of the mood whose startup chain selected it. The files have no
separate section, directive, key, or value syntax.
.PP
Commands, comments, quoting, expansion, redirection, functions, and builtins use
the syntax defined by
.BR kosh (1).
Startup discovery, loading order, suppression, and error handling are also
defined there.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/koshrc
This is the system configuration file for an interactive
.B kosh
mood.
.TP
.I ~/.koshrc
This is the user configuration file for an interactive
.B kosh
mood.
.TP
.I /etc/profile
This is the system login configuration file.
.TP
.I ~/.profile
This is the user POSIX login configuration file and the last Bash login
candidate.
.TP
.I ~/.bash_profile
This is the first user Bash login candidate.
.TP
.I ~/.bash_login
This is the second user Bash login candidate.
.TP
.I "/etc/bash/bashrc or /etc/bash.bashrc"
The first readable path is the system configuration file for an interactive
non-login Bash mood.
.TP
.I ~/.bashrc
This is the default user configuration file for an interactive non-login Bash
mood.
.TP
.I /usr/share/bash-completion/bash_completion
This file supplies Bash programmable completion when the preceding Bash startup
chain sourced an rc file. An existing default completion specification or
BASH_COMPLETION_VERSINFO suppresses this file.
.PP
The
.BR \-\-rcfile ,
.BR \-\-init-file ,
.BR ENV ,
and
.B BASH_ENV
interfaces may select another pathname. Their conditions and expansion rules
are defined in
.BR kosh (1).
.SH SYNTAX
The complete file is shell source. LF and CRLF terminate a line. A CRLF pair is
one newline. A lone carriage return remains source text.
.PP
A number sign begins a shell comment where the shell lexical rules recognize a
comment. Assignments, shell options, functions, aliases, and commands take
effect in the shell that sources the file. A sourced configuration file may
select a runtime mood with
.B set \-\-mood
or request another startup chain with
.BR "set \-\-init\-moods" .
Recursive initialization of a mood already being sourced is skipped.
.SH ERRORS
A missing optional file, custom rc file, or BASH_ENV file is skipped. An
existing custom rc or BASH_ENV file that cannot be read produces a diagnostic
and is skipped. An unreadable ENV file is skipped without that diagnostic.
Syntax and execution errors use the ordinary shell diagnostics defined by
.BR kosh (1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kosh (1)
